  "readme": "**Author :** 5argon,  https://arkham-starter.com\n\nI'm pretty content with the \"Starter's Insert\" design for Core 2026 as a generic template for most beginners. But there's one thing it can't do: It can't store an act / agenda stand (not longer than the long edge of A4 paper). I've been playing with the slitted wooden block card stand for years and I can't left it out of my setup. (It holds act, agenda, and the vertical scenario reference card in one block.)\n\nSo I tried adding that and it's a wrench that ruins everything in the \"Starter's Insert\" design! That insert was based on the box was able to hold 2x 100 mm wide columns side by side with a little leftover column. With that column now widened to contain the card stand, it is now impossible to have 2 columns. I had to give up something.\n\nNaturally I went sideways instead. In this design, there are only 2 card storage **A1 and A2** divided equally. Each one can fit all Core 2026 encounter cards plus 3 Brethren of Ash scenarios, or large amount of random basic weakness. (Fits all basic weakness in complete Chapter 1 collection.) And so deck building player cards shall be somewhere else. Personally I'd also not store Core 2026 encounter cards here as I prefer them in the campaign box instead. I can use the space for dices and other custom things, or maybe the active player's decks.\n\nThe 4 stacked removable token trays in \"Starter's Insert\" design makes their comeback in a slightly larger size in **B1 and B2**. Since a smaller one in Starter's Insert was proven to be able to store every tokens except chaos tokens, this one is strictly better. The **B3** narrow slot is for tucking in your active chaos bag with active chaos tokens inside. This slot your hand can't reach the bottom so I think this is the best use of it.\n\nThe **C** slot stores all remaining inactive chaos tokens. This is also a removable box so you can take it out and pour the contents. You can also not make the removable box, but you'd have to dig inside the core box.\n\nLastly **D1 and D2** are removable box that serve as a padding for the card stand to sit above them and press down their shared lid. The inner height is 2 cm so you can store some dices up to that size.",
  "secondaryBase": true
